<title>SWITZERLAND: Britain's Clarke still doubts EMU date.</title>
<headline>Britain's Clarke still doubts EMU date.</headline>
<text>
<p>DAVOS, Switzerland, Jan 31 (Reuter) Britain's Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said he remained convinced that European Monetary Union (EMU) would not go into effect on January 1 1999.</p>
<p>But he told reporters that he thought it would be implemented not long after the target date.</p>
<p>&quot;It is indeed still my opinion that it will not start in January 1999,&quot; said Clarke, speaking at a news conference at the World Economic Forum in Davos.</p>
<p>But he said there was a heavy commitment among member countries of the European Union to the project.</p>
<p>&quot;So I think it is more likely than not that it (implementation) will be not long thereafter,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Davos Newsroom 41-81 413 14 49</p>
</text>
